{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# J5 — A Dockerized Jira harness as the Data Center verification oracle\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nThere is no way to buy a Jira Data Center license to test against: Atlassian ended new DC purchases on\n30 March 2026 and no longer issues DC trial licenses. There is also **no official OpenAPI/Swagger spec for Jira\nDC** — Atlassian publishes only WADL, and the long-standing requests for one (JRASERVER-65954, JRASERVER-68539)\nremain open — so spec-driven contract testing is unavailable. Cloud's v3 swagger is not a substitute: different\nauth, ADF vs wiki markup, accountId vs name. Without an oracle, a DC adapter is unverifiable except against\nfakes that encode our own assumptions.\n\n## Approach\n\nUse the **purpose-built test image that pycontribs/jira publishes for exactly this problem**:\n`pycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1`, run as `docker run -dit -p 2990:2990 --name jira\npycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1`, reachable at `http://localhost:2990/jira` with the project's documented\ncredentials (`CI_JIRA_ADMIN=admin` / `CI_JIRA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin`, `CI_JIRA_USER=jira_user` /\n`CI_JIRA_USER_PASSWORD=jira`). It is a pinned, pullable image carrying its own license, so it is unaffected by\nthe DC trial shutdown, and it is the substrate the most widely used Python Jira client validates itself\nagainst. Jira 8.17.1 is **≥ 8.14**, the release that introduced Personal Access Tokens, so the PAT bearer auth\nthe DC transport uses is exercised for real.\n\n**Stated limitation, deliberately accepted:** 8.17.1 is older than the version a client such as CMS is likely\nrunning, so this harness proves REST v2 protocol semantics, not deployment-specific behavior (workflow names,\ncustom fields, permission schemes, user directories). Closing that gap requires access to the real instance and\nis tracked separately as ticket `9895-ac7d-4276-4f08`; this story's README records the exact image tag so that\ncomparison has a baseline.\n\nAdd `tests/live_jira_dc/` with a compose file, a readiness probe that polls until the instance answers REST,\nand a fixture that provisions a scratch project and tears down everything it created. **Every test in the\ndirectory carries the existing `integration` marker** — not a new custom marker — because `make test` runs\n`pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"` (`Makefile:154`), so the suite is excluded by construction with\nno Makefile change and no filter-expression edit.\n\nTeardown follows ADR 0037 §3, which **prohibits post-deletion search-index assertions** because Jira's index\nlags creates and deletes by an unbounded interval and can return stale results either way. So the teardown\noracle is not \"query the project and find it empty\": it asserts each delete call's HTTP status and then polls\neach issue's **direct REST endpoint** (`/rest/api/2/issue/{key}`) until it returns 404, which is index-independent.\n\n**Alternative rejected: fixtures and a stateful fake alone.** rebar's test-design standard allows a verified\nfake for external-service mapping, but a fake verified only against fixtures we recorded cannot falsify\nassumptions we never thought to record — transitions, permission errors, link direction. The fake is still\nbuilt (J6 uses it for fast unit tests); this story gives it something real to be verified against.\n\n**Alternative rejected: reusing pycontribs/jira's test assertions as the oracle.** Their tests assert their\nclient's behavior, not rebar's field mapping. The reusable asset is the image and harness pattern, which is\nwhat this story takes.\n\n**Alternative rejected: the Atlassian SDK's `atlas-run-standalone`.** It also yields a licensed local Jira, but\nit needs the full SDK toolchain and its licenses are short-lived (3-day timebombs requiring `atlas-mvn clean`\nrecycling), which is hostile to repeatable CI. A pinned Docker image has neither problem.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/live_jira_dc/docker-compose.yml`, `conftest.py`, `README.md` (new) — image pinned to\n  `pycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1`.\n- `tests/live_jira_dc/test_harness_smoke.py` (new).\n- `Makefile` — a `jira-dc-up` target only; the `test:` target is NOT modified (the `integration` marker is\n  already excluded by its existing `-m` expression at `Makefile:154`).\n\n## Testing\n\nReal-external-service tier by construction — this story *is* the harness. Its own oracle is that the harness\nstarts, is usable, and provably cleans up.\n\n- happy path: the harness starts, the readiness probe reports REST answering, and a smoke test creates and\n  reads back one issue through raw REST v2.\n- auth path: a Personal Access Token minted on the 8.17.1 instance authenticates a request via\n  `Authorization: Bearer`, proving the DC auth mode the transport will use is exercised, not assumed.\n- teardown oracle (index-independent, per ADR 0037 §3): after a deliberately failing test, every issue the\n  fixture created returns 404 from its direct `/rest/api/2/issue/{key}` endpoint, and each delete call's HTTP\n  status was 2xx. Search is never consulted.\n- gating oracle: `pytest --collect-only -m \"not integration and not external\"` collects zero tests from\n  `tests/live_jira_dc/`.\n- failure path: with the instance down, the marked suite fails with a clear \"harness not running\" message from\n  the readiness probe rather than a raw connection traceback.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docker run -dit -p 2990:2990 pycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1` pulls and starts, and the readiness\n      probe reports REST v2 answering at `http://localhost:2990/jira`\n- [ ] a smoke test creates and reads back an issue via REST v2, and a PAT-authenticated request succeeds\n- [ ] after an intentionally failing test run, every created issue returns 404 from its direct issue endpoint\n      (no search query used anywhere in teardown verification)\n- [ ] `pytest --collect-only -m \"not integration and not external\"` reports 0 tests collected from\n      `tests/live_jira_dc/`, and `git diff Makefile` shows no change to the `test:` target\n- [ ] `tests/live_jira_dc/README.md` records the pinned image tag and states the version-drift limitation,\n      naming ticket `9895-ac7d-4276-4f08` as where real-instance validation is tracked"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785011212694078001,"uuid":"46e6e202-2ce9-4ca5-9792-c4d46dd9c2a5"}